ion in sub-Saharan Africa.</article-title><source>Parasitol Today</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>105</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>11</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0169-4758(99)01396-4</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10322323</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15. </label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Central Board of Health, Ministry of Health, Government of Republic of Zambia (GRZ).</collab> Zambia 2004 antenatal clinic sentinel surveillance. Lusaka (Zambia): GRZ; <year>2007</year></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>Severe falciparum malaria. World Health Organization, communicable diseases cluster.</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>94</volume>(<issue>Suppl 1</issue>):<fpage>S1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11103309</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17. </label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Central Board of Health, Ministry of Health, Government of Republic of Zambia (GRZ).</collab> Zambia. Management of antiretroviral therapy. A reference manual for health workers. Lusaka (Zambia): GRZ; <year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Janossy</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Jani</surname> <given-names>I</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>G&#x000f6;hde</surname> <given-names>W</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Affordable CD4(+) T-cell counts on &#x02018;single-platform&#x02019; flow cytometers I. Primary CD4 gating.</article-title><source>Br J Haematol</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>111</volume>:<fpage>1198</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>208</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2141.2000.02433.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11167762</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19. </label><citation